  "term": "corpus callosum agenesis",
  "definition": "Corpus callosum agenesis is a birth defect in which the corpus callosum is partly or completely absent. It can occur on its own or as part of a broader syndrome, and may be associated with problems in movement-related skills and intellectual disability that vary in severity.",
